    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0400" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/953</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-30T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5930. Your 7782.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d361-f1"/> For your information. The
                    conclusion of a separate peace with Turkey is regarded as chimerical and of
                    questionable advantage even if it could be accomplished. At the conference which
                    closes the war arrangements must be made with regard to Constantinople which
                    could not be made if peace were first declared with Turkey. At the present time
                    separate peace could only be made which would preclude any radical changes of
                    control over Constantinople and the Straits. It appears, therefore, to this
                    Government that the only advantage to be gained by separate peace with Turkey
                    now would be to prevent the bargains of the Allies with regard to Asia Minor
                    from being carried out at the end of the war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
